# What Happens When You Open Chrome After Login?

You double-click Chrome.

OS:

Find chrome.exe
        ↓
Load into RAM
        ↓
Create Process
        ↓
Allocate Memory
        ↓
Give CPU Time
        ↓
Chrome Starts

Notice something important:

👉 Chrome starts only because the OS is already running.

Without the OS being loaded and active, Chrome cannot run at all.

Does the Operating System start immediately after pressing the power button?

Answer:

No.

First BIOS/UEFI runs, performs hardware checks, loads the bootloader, and then the bootloader loads the OS kernel into memory. After that, the operating system starts.
