New State

Naya process create hua hai.

Ready State

Process CPU ka wait kar raha hai.

Running State

CPU process ko execute kar raha hai.

Waiting State

Process kisi event/I/O ka wait kar raha hai.

Terminated State

Process khatam ho gaya hai.

Interview Answer (30 Seconds)

A process moves through five main states: New, Ready, Running, Waiting (Blocked), and Terminated. 
A newly created process enters the Ready queue, waits for CPU allocation, executes in the Running state, may move to Waiting for I/O operations,
returns to Ready after the event completes, and finally enters the Terminated state when execution finishes.

